// Arguments that are not a list are an error, not silently "no arguments". A
// bare string here used to run the command with the string ignored — a command
// that never did what was asked, reporting success. (The block-where-a-list-
// belongs spelling of this mistake is now a parse error; see
// syntax/comma_in_block_is_rejected.)
! @process.run("sh", "-c exit 17", ⟨⟩)?
